-- ============================================================================
-- FC9 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Corrosion & Integrity, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE LEVERS AND THE ALLOWANCE. The wetting regime as a
-- dropdown that can take the rate to zero, and the oil-wet zero that withholds
-- its category and its life; efficiency and availability as two inputs, and
-- the time average that eats the wall; this module's own wall shear, its own
-- friction factor and the discontinuity at its branch switch, named beside the
-- line sizing course's different correlation; the shear verdict acting on the
-- rate, with the credited rate reported beside it; the allowance divided by a
-- rate, a zero rate that is not a pass, and three apps that use one word with
-- no link between them; and which film governs, from a ratio that needs no
-- pressure.
--
-- THE LESSON THIS TIER EXISTS TO TEACH. A 95 percent corrosion inhibitor
-- running 80 percent of the time is not a 95 percent solution. The engine
-- takes the two percentages separately and the metal-loss ratio against the
-- datasheet number is a straight line in the availability.
--
-- The Professional capstone grades the corrosion inhibitor arithmetic and the
-- allowance arithmetic on a rate STATED from a two-year ultrasonic survey, so
-- no correlation constant, no fugacity coefficient and no held threshold is in
-- any graded chain. Nothing downstream of the protective-film factor is graded
-- anywhere in this course.
-- ============================================================================

